[36.259011, "o", "  qwen3.6-35b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Interesting — `ensurepip` says pip is installed in site-packages, but Pyt…\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/ 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/ 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: cat /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/top_level.txt 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cat /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/top_l…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The `pip` package directory itself is missing — only the `.dist-info` met…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info"]
[36.259037, "o", " 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info 2>…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\nFixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` package's source code (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`) was missing from your system Python installation. Only the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) remained, so `pip3` would crash with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'` on every"]
[36.259048, "o", " invocation.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which reinstalled the full pip package (source code + metadata) into site-packages.\r\n\r\n**Verification:** `pip3 --version` now reports `pip 24.3.1`, and a dry-run `pip install requests` confirms packages can be installed successfully.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=17 surface=de1fadd2f308\r\n"]
